@integrations/skills/sigil/external-guidance-evidence.sigil import { ExternalGuidanceEvidence }

component SigilStandardsReview {
  goal {
    Classify repository and external-guidance evidence, assess applicable
    standards, and present scoped findings without replacing project decisions or
    approval.
  }

  interface {
EvidenceReview {
      separates observed behavior, documented intent, user-confirmed intent,
      unresolved ambiguity, suspected accidental behavior, and external guidance
    }

StandardsReview {
      assesses applicable authoritative guidance and classifies findings before
      proposing informed semantic changes
    }
  }
}

expand SigilStandardsReview {
  state {
EvidenceReview {
      Evidence is classified as observed behavior, documented intent, user-confirmed
      intent, unresolved ambiguity, suspected accidental behavior, or external
      guidance.
    }

StandardsReview {
      A researched finding is compatible guidance, a potential conflict, a definite
      conflict, unverifiable guidance, or non-applicable.
    }
  }

  logic {
EvidenceReview {
      Inspect relevant Sigil, implementation, tests, documentation, manifests, and
      executable configuration.

      Keep every evidence category distinct in analysis and proposals.

      Report contradictions instead of silently choosing one source as intent.
    }

StandardsReview {
      Use ApplicabilityAssessment and EvidencePacket from ExternalGuidanceEvidence on
      every Sigil review and acquire required or recommended authoritative research.

      Verify the currency and environment match of evidence created during design
      conversation before reusing it.

      Classify each current finding and present compatible changes as exact proposed
      semantic units.

      Preserve current Sigil and request a decision when guidance potentially or
      definitely conflicts.
    }
  }

  constraints {
EvidenceReview {
      Code is evidence of current behavior, not proof of desired behavior or
      rationale.

      Suspected accidental behavior does not become a contract without user
      confirmation.
    }

StandardsReview {
      Design conversation shows directly relevant source identity with
      evidence-informed recommendations.

      Standards review records complete source details and maps findings to their
      supporting evidence.

      Approved Sigil may retain a source identifier and applicable version only when
      needed to reconstruct material rationale or its revisit condition.

      Source URLs and full bibliographic records remain outside Sigil unless a
      separate policy is approved.

      Approved additions are written as project decisions rather than claims of
      certification.

      A conflict never silently overrides approved Sigil.
    }
  }

  decisions {
StandardsReview {
      Decision: Consume shared ExternalGuidanceEvidence while retaining standards
      review authority over finding classification and gate consequences.

      Scope: Governs standards-aware semantic review; excludes evidence acquisition
      mechanics and design-conversation recommendation policy.

      Trade-offs: Reused evidence must receive a separate currency and applicability
      verification.

      Design issues addressed: Shared evidence should not allow its producer or an
      earlier design conversation to determine approval consequences.

      Consequences: Research remains reusable while standards review independently
      owns conflicts, compliance language, and blocking outcomes.

      Revisit when: Evidence classification and workflow approval become one
      intentionally governed component.
    }
  }

  cases {
EvidenceReview {
      Conflicting code, tests, and documentation are reported for user decision
      rather than silently reconciled.
    }

StandardsReview {
      Unavailable compliance-critical guidance blocks implementation while low-risk
      unverifiable guidance is reported for explicit acceptance.
    }
  }
}
